WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.075
Next, run the ServiceNow script's
own fifteen tests in Node,

2
00:00:04.075 --> 00:00:06.087
the rules the Python mirrors.

3
00:00:06.087 --> 00:00:08.650
Then run the drift reconciliation over the

4
00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:11.426
fixtures and check every
payload it would post.

5
00:00:11.426 --> 00:00:12.812
Twelve are accepted.

6
00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:17.525
Three carry the warning: two missing
identities and the unauthorized write.

7
00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:20.798
The three orphan accounts
are decided by a person too,

8
00:00:20.798 --> 00:00:25.187
but their payloads already say what a
re-read must find, so they don't warn.

9
00:00:25.187 --> 00:00:30.576
Notice Erin's two attribute drifts
in Entra ID, department and manager.

10
00:00:30.576 --> 00:00:32.238
They now have separate keys.

11
00:00:32.238 --> 00:00:34.637
Before Chapter 4's fix, they shared one,

12
00:00:34.637 --> 00:00:37.870
and the second would have
vanished into the first.
